<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαλμός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pin</i> or <i>thole</i> to
			which the Greek oar was fastened by the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπωτήρ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				7.42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				376
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1598
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				1347
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπομόχλιον ὁ ς. γίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mech.</u>
					850b11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ σκαλμὸν ἐρέσσειν</span>
			(opp. <i>paddle</i>) <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Ind.</u>
				27.5
			</span></i>:—of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πριαπίσκος</span> in the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάθρον
				Ἱπποκράτους</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.26.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. θρανίτης</span>
			<i>a bank</i> or <i>bench</i> of rowers, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαλισμός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1631.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>.</div>
